# AWS Production Architecture

Production runs on AWS with CloudFront, an Application Load Balancer, and a single EC2 host running Docker Compose.

Before changing deployment, Docker, nginx, frontend API URL handling, CORS, object storage/media, or AWS documentation, read `docs/AWS-infrastructure_setup_documentation.md`.

Key invariants:
- Frontend public URLs are `https://futboligy.com` and `https://www.futboligy.com`.
- API traffic must use `https://api.futboligy.com/api`, not relative `/api` from the frontend domain.
- EC2 Compose runs `proxy` (nginx, routes `Host: api.futboligy.com` to the API, everything else to the UI), `ui` (Next.js standalone), `api`, `postgres`, and `migrator`.
- The EC2 instance has no inbound SSH; deploys and shell access go through AWS SSM.
- Production media uses private S3 (`futboligy-prod-media`) with presigned upload/read URLs.
- `media.futboligy.com` CloudFront delivery is future/planned unless the docs and code say otherwise.
